WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.245
What if importing were a board game?

00:00:02.544 --> 00:00:04.007
Each square is a step.

00:00:04.306 --> 00:00:06.663
And some of them send you back to the start.

00:00:06.713 --> 00:00:07.997
You roll the dice.

00:00:08.095 --> 00:00:10.425
The factory produces and sends the documents.

00:00:10.639 --> 00:00:13.179
One mismatch, and the cargo never ships.

00:00:13.277 --> 00:00:20.546
Surprise card: the shipment date on the invoice is the day the order entered the system, not the actual departure.

00:00:20.845 --> 00:00:23.312
Plan by it and you get the arrival wrong.

00:00:23.611 --> 00:00:24.958
Paying the freight yourself?

00:00:25.342 --> 00:00:26.854
The quote has an expiry date.

00:00:26.904 --> 00:00:28.832
Once it expires, the price goes up.

00:00:28.930 --> 00:00:31.487
Now, the most expensive card in the game.

00:00:31.537 --> 00:00:36.009
For some products, ANVISA only accepts batches made after the import approval.

00:00:36.308 --> 00:00:38.626
A batch made before it was shipped.

00:00:38.725 --> 00:00:42.101
It arrived in Brazil... and had to go back.

00:00:42.315 --> 00:00:46.914
The lesson: check batch and manufacturing date before approving the shipment.

00:00:47.012 --> 00:00:50.698
Once the plane takes off, there is almost never time to cancel.

00:00:50.748 --> 00:00:55.969
Demo products without registration go back too: they only enter temporarily.

00:00:56.184 --> 00:00:59.041
And never on the same plane as registered products.

00:00:59.255 --> 00:01:00.972
If one gets stuck, everything stops.

00:01:01.070 --> 00:01:02.403
Landed in Guarulhos?

00:01:02.453 --> 00:01:03.447
It is not yours yet.

00:01:03.497 --> 00:01:06.714
The cargo waits in the bonded warehouse, paying a daily fee.

00:01:07.012 --> 00:01:09.411
The import declaration is assigned a channel.

00:01:09.461 --> 00:01:10.688
Green, it moves on.

00:01:10.738 --> 00:01:13.010
Yellow, document review.

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:15.051
Red, physical inspection.

00:01:15.265 --> 00:01:16.662
Damage on arrival?

00:01:16.712 --> 00:01:21.215
Answer the customs broker within 24 hours and keep the evidence for the insurance.

00:01:21.515 --> 00:01:22.365
Released?

00:01:22.855 --> 00:01:25.845
Without the inbound invoice, the daily fee keeps running.

00:01:25.895 --> 00:01:27.759
Only then does the product become stock.

00:01:28.143 --> 00:01:35.136
Importing is a chain of deadlines: every document requirement turns into storage days and stockout risk.

00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:36.315
What about you?

00:01:36.365 --> 00:01:38.746
Which square has sent you back to the start?
